WEBVTT


00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.504
¶ When our weeping's over ¶


00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:10.099
¶ He will bid us welcome ¶


00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.906
¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶


00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.539
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.015
¶ Bringing
in the sheaves ¶


00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.610
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:23.143
- ¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶


00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:25.713
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.659
- ¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:31.219
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:33.629
¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶


00:00:33.665 --> 00:00:38.034
- ¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.631
Now you've got drought here.


00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:44.302
You've got drought


00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.709
right here in Gatlin, Nebraska.


00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:49.976
And there's not gonna be
no harvest this year


00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:54.111
not in this Lord's year
of 1963, there ain't.


00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.621
- And say why.
- Sin.


00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.316
Say that louder.


00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:00.416
Sin!


00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:02.324
Oh, we drown in sin here,


00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:05.091
- and there's no rain for our corn.


00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.564
- And why is that?


00:01:07.599 --> 00:01:10.864
Because of
all of the adults in this world.


00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:14.634
God has spoken to me
in a dream.


00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:16.300
And in that dream


00:01:16.341 --> 00:01:19.936
He said that
all adults are sinners!


00:01:19.978 --> 00:01:23.311
He said there's
not a soul here in Gatlin


00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:25.316
over the age of 19


00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.252
who isn't wallowing in sin,
loving it, even as they drown


00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.756
- like pigs in a mire.


00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.985
It says in the Good Book,


00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:36.995
"Suffer the children
to come unto me."


00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.759
And if this town has any hope,


00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:43.325
it's in you young people.


00:01:43.368 --> 00:01:45.233
And so I want you to shout it out!


00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.000
Sin!


00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.109
But, brothers and sisters,


00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:57.638
we know the old ways of God,
isn't it so?


00:01:57.683 --> 00:02:00.243
We know there's
a God of the Old Testament,


00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:01.946
as well as the New


00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:05.855
the God of sacrifice,


00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:09.588
the God who walked
on the face of the earth,


00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:12.722
He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


00:02:12.764 --> 00:02:15.665
He Who Walks Behind The Rows.


00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.693
He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:21.069
God does speak to me
in my dreams,


00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:25.566
and God has told me
that it is now our time


00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.738
time to make sacrifice,


00:02:27.779 --> 00:02:29.610
time to kill!


00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:40.016
Now the Good Book does say
that a child shall lead them.


00:02:40.058 --> 00:02:44.154
So do what God tells me
in my dreams to tell to you,


00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:49.998
and never go without water
or be hungry again!


00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:52.333
Praise God.
Praise the Lord.


00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:55.204
Praise God. Praise the Lord.


00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.606
Praise God!


00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.385
Hail Mary, full of grace,


00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:13.914
- help me win this stock car race.


00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.223
All right. Boogie.


00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:21.694
¶ Riding on the road
to nowhere ¶


00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:26.136
- ¶ Trying to keep love alive... ¶
- Turn it down!


00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:27.832
Do you want to break
my eardrums?


00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:30.433
Yes, Vicky.
Whatever you say.


00:03:30.475 --> 00:03:32.500
...who was
cited for reckless driving.


00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:36.947
¶ Be happy
if you'll just stay with me ¶


00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.179
¶ I know everything
will be all right ¶


00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.349
¶ We'll laugh and we'll sing
all through the night... ¶


00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.483
- Too loud, Burt!
- What's that?


00:03:48.493 --> 00:03:50.324
- You play it like that


00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.353
- just to get under my skin.
- Oh, come on.


00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:54.524
Your paranoia is
showing again, Vicky.


00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:57.228
Sometimes, I wonder
how I ended up married to you.


00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.635
By saying two little words.


00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:03.402
Shut up.


00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.004
Nebraska.


00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:27.855
I'm hungry. Where are we?


00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.533
Nebraska.


00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.061
Yes, I know that.


00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:37.075
But where in the hell are we?
Where's the lunch stop?


00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:40.169
You've got the road atlas.
You should look it up.


00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.146
You still remember
how to read, don't you?


00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.547
Such a comedian.
Is that why we got off the interstate,


00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:49.213
to look at 60 miles of corn and listen
to the wit and wisdom of Burt?


00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:53.122
Just get off it, Vicky!
Will you just get off it?!


00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:01.798
¶ Oh, well, they call me ¶


00:05:01.833 --> 00:05:04.825
- ¶ Sergeant Evil... ¶


00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:10.172
¶ But I just played a part ¶


00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:15.271
¶ They think
my eyes are tearing ¶


00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:21.651
¶ But they don't know me
at all, yeah! ¶


00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:31.188
- I'm sorry.


00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.857
It's all right. It's fine.


00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:37.699
It's just that I've driven so far
on the interstate 1500 miles


00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:40.364
- and since you won't drive, l
- You know I get migraines


00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:43.067
- when I drive for a long time.
- I know you do. I know, okay?


00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:45.576
That's why I asked you to navigate
for me on these secondary roads,


00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.635
and you said you would.


00:05:54.986 --> 00:05:57.113
- Well?
- Where did we get off the interstate?


00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:59.248
Back in Grand lsland.


00:06:00.592 --> 00:06:02.822
The next town is...


00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:06.194
Gatlin.
It's about 10 miles.


00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:17.303
A wide space in the road.
Do you suppose we can go there


00:06:17.342 --> 00:06:19.970
and get something to eat?
Or does the almighty schedule say


00:06:20.011 --> 00:06:22.070
we have to go on until 2:00
like we did yesterday?


00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.878
All right. You know what?
I have about had it with you.


00:06:27.018 --> 00:06:29.782
As far as I am concerned,
we can call it quits right now.


00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:31.948
We can just turn around and see
that lawyer you wanted to see


00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.787
- because I have had it
- Watch out!


00:06:33.825 --> 00:06:36.259
- No!


00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:50.471
Burt!


00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.475
A dog tell me it was a dog.


00:06:58.216 --> 00:07:00.275
It was a boy.
It was a little boy.


00:07:00.318 --> 00:07:02.445
He ran out of the corn.


00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:08.149
He's dead.
He's dead, isn't he?


00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:10.184
Oh, yeah.


00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:17.667
Congratulations, tiger.


00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:38.555
It's manslaughter!


00:07:41.526 --> 00:07:45.690
That's what they call it!
You took your eyes off the road!


00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.459
Well, don't you
wanna come see


00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:50.195
so you can tell
all your NRA buddies


00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:53.170
what you bagged
in Nebraska, huh?!


00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:58.632
Don't you wanna come
and see?


00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:03.070
What are you gonna do?!


00:08:05.784 --> 00:08:07.684
What are you going to do?


00:08:09.554 --> 00:08:11.385
Answer me!


00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:14.415
Answer me, you


00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:19.029
Answer me when I talk to you!


00:08:20.298 --> 00:08:22.289
Look at me!


00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:25.593
Look at me!


00:08:31.109 --> 00:08:35.068
How'd you handle it
over in Nam, huh?


00:08:35.113 --> 00:08:38.549
How'd you handle it in the hooches?


00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:40.744
What do you use?
Grease guns, right?


00:08:40.785 --> 00:08:42.480
Grease guns and Zippos!


00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.921
Settle down.
You're hysterical.


00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:47.948
Oh, tell me. You crapped out.


00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:51.861
Big Vietnam War hero, huh?


00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:55.333
Purple Heart
and all that, huh?


00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:58.859
Come on, John Wayne!
What are you gonna do?!


00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.202
It's no time to go Section 8!


00:09:01.239 --> 00:09:03.104
You ran that little boy down.


00:09:03.141 --> 00:09:05.837
He was just a little boy,
you ran him down


00:09:05.877 --> 00:09:08.539
and you can't


00:09:21.826 --> 00:09:23.953
You're going to jail.


00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.025
- You're going to jail.
- Yeah?


00:09:27.065 --> 00:09:29.056
- Yeah.
- You're rabid.


00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.227
Okay. It's taken me
all this time to figure it out.


00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:33.499
You've got a terminal case
of rabies.


00:09:33.538 --> 00:09:35.267
Shut up.


00:09:45.216 --> 00:09:47.616
- What are you doing?
- Turning him over.


00:09:47.652 --> 00:09:51.053
- No. You're not supposed to touch
- I wanna see what I did.


00:09:52.791 --> 00:09:56.158
- I'm sorry about this, fella.
- I don't wanna look.


00:10:08.406 --> 00:10:11.967
His carotid artery and jugular vein
have been severed.


00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:16.138
His throat's been cut.


00:10:17.449 --> 00:10:19.474
Somebody scragged this kid


00:10:19.517 --> 00:10:22.680
bayonet, maybe a kitchen knife,
a cleaver I don't know.


00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.712
It sure wasn't
a two-dollar buck.


00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:31.857
You don't go to any more Kiwanis
meetings after your throat's been cut.


00:10:31.896 --> 00:10:33.591
I sure learned that
in the jungle.


00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:36.794
You get 20, maybe 30 seconds,
before you


00:10:36.835 --> 00:10:39.998
- That little boy is dead.
- Yeah.


00:10:40.038 --> 00:10:41.198
- You ran him down.
- Yeah.


00:10:41.239 --> 00:10:43.104
- And you killed him!
- Sure, I ran him down,


00:10:43.141 --> 00:10:45.041
but I didn't kill him.


00:10:45.076 --> 00:10:47.601
Look. Go on, look at him.


00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:49.238
I haven't gone crazy.
His throat's been cut.


00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.908
Why would anybody cut
a little boy's throat? Huh, why?


00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.350
You like the idea that I killed him
too much to let it go?


00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:57.287
- No. Of course not.
- Just look!


00:10:59.257 --> 00:11:02.055
- Please look.


00:11:10.602 --> 00:11:12.194
- Hey hey hey.
- Oh!


00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:16.037
- Don't faint. Look at me.
- Okay.


00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:18.599
Don't look around.
Don't look around.


00:11:18.643 --> 00:11:22.204
- There's so much blood.
- His throat's been cut,


00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:24.147
and that corn over there
is all bent and twisted.


00:11:24.182 --> 00:11:25.376
- Where?
- Don't look around.


00:11:25.417 --> 00:11:27.385
Ow!


00:11:27.419 --> 00:11:30.081
Don't act suspicious.


00:11:30.121 --> 00:11:31.520
Okay.


00:11:31.556 --> 00:11:33.456
- Okay?
- Yeah.


00:11:34.492 --> 00:11:36.687
Now we're gonna cover
this boy up


00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:40.687
- and we're gonna put him in the trunk.


00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:43.292
- I'm sorry about this, Vicky...
- Okay.


00:11:43.334 --> 00:11:46.132
-...but we've gotta do this.
- Okay.


00:11:51.076 --> 00:11:54.876
Sure. Yeah.


00:11:54.913 --> 00:11:57.143
That didn't cut his throat


00:11:57.182 --> 00:11:59.150
not all ragged
and jagged like this.


00:11:59.184 --> 00:12:03.280
No army sergeant ever showed
the finer points of hand-to-hand combat


00:12:03.321 --> 00:12:05.482
to this poor boy's murderer.


00:12:05.523 --> 00:12:08.959
No, he was as good as dead
when I hit him.


00:12:17.368 --> 00:12:19.529
Okay.


00:12:26.177 --> 00:12:27.906
Get in.


00:12:27.946 --> 00:12:31.143
No. Driver's side.


00:12:31.182 --> 00:12:33.673
- You want me to drive?
- No. I want you to start the car


00:12:33.718 --> 00:12:36.152
and wait for me.
I'm gonna go take a look.


00:12:36.187 --> 00:12:39.179
I can see blood on the corn
where the boy came out.


00:12:39.224 --> 00:12:41.886
I think I saw something else.
It's hard to tell from the road,


00:12:41.926 --> 00:12:44.360
but you can hide an army in there.


00:12:44.395 --> 00:12:46.386
The Vietcong sure did.


00:12:46.431 --> 00:12:50.162
In the paddies of course,
not the corn like jungles.


00:12:51.503 --> 00:12:53.403
Scragged, right?


00:12:53.438 --> 00:12:55.099
- Someone scragged him?
- Yeah.


00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.007
Sometimes, I think you'd sell your soul
to the devil for it never to have ended.


00:12:58.042 --> 00:12:59.976
That way you could go on
doing sweeps and smoking dope


00:13:00.011 --> 00:13:02.479
for the rest of your life 'cause
that was the high point of your life,


00:13:02.514 --> 00:13:04.175
wasn't it, Burt?
Good old Vietnam, right?


00:13:04.215 --> 00:13:07.810
This isn't one of your damn
consciousness-raising groups, Vicky.


00:13:07.852 --> 00:13:10.116
Now get in the car.
That's an order.


00:13:10.155 --> 00:13:11.918
Screw your orders.


00:13:13.291 --> 00:13:15.759
Vicky, would you just do it?!


00:13:23.868 --> 00:13:25.358
What's up with the gun?


00:13:25.403 --> 00:13:28.065
His throat was cut, right?


00:13:28.106 --> 00:13:31.337
They're probably gone,
but I don't wanna take any chances.


00:13:31.376 --> 00:13:35.039
Now get in the car,
keep the engine running


00:13:35.079 --> 00:13:37.411
and you'd better bug out
should anyone come out of there,


00:13:37.448 --> 00:13:39.973
no matter how innocent he,
she or they may look, okay?


00:13:40.018 --> 00:13:42.077
Do you understand?


00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.350
I don't wanna sit in the car
all by myself.


00:13:44.389 --> 00:13:47.950
At this point,
I don't really care what you want.


00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.394
How did I end up married
to a son of a bitch like you


00:13:51.429 --> 00:13:53.954
in the first place, huh?
I wonder about that.


00:13:55.433 --> 00:13:57.264
I wonder about that a lot.


00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:01.437
So do l, babe.


00:14:02.941 --> 00:14:04.602
I'm scared.


00:14:09.113 --> 00:14:11.172
Is that all right, sir?


00:14:11.216 --> 00:14:13.309
Is it all right for me
to be scared, sir?


00:14:13.351 --> 00:14:15.251
That's fine by me.


00:17:27.612 --> 00:17:30.911
- Oh, God.


00:17:39.557 --> 00:17:42.685
Hey! Mr. Comedian!


00:17:46.497 --> 00:17:48.260
Where are you?


00:17:50.535 --> 00:17:53.003
It's not funny!


00:17:55.139 --> 00:17:57.664
Burt!


00:17:57.708 --> 00:18:00.370
I told you to stay in the car.


00:18:00.411 --> 00:18:02.504
I thought somebody was watching me.
I looked behind me


00:18:02.547 --> 00:18:04.538
- and I couldn't see you.
- Get in.


00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:07.642
I should've tied a string
around the antenna.


00:18:08.786 --> 00:18:10.686
I got lost in there for awhile.


00:18:10.721 --> 00:18:13.212
It's a good thing you called
when you did. Push over.


00:18:16.294 --> 00:18:19.127
Here, grab this.


00:18:19.163 --> 00:18:21.256
What is it?


00:18:21.299 --> 00:18:23.426
Is that is that blood?
Is that his blood?


00:18:23.468 --> 00:18:26.335
- Yeah, I guess so. Grab it.
- No!


00:19:20.758 --> 00:19:22.316
I was scared.


00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:24.328
Uh-huh.


00:19:24.362 --> 00:19:26.023
Afraid I was afraid.


00:19:26.063 --> 00:19:29.521
You went into the corn and it felt
like somebody was watching me.


00:19:29.567 --> 00:19:32.536
Well, maybe someone was.


00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.936
You know what I'm talking about.


00:19:34.972 --> 00:19:38.601
Someone was there, all right?
I could feel it too.


00:19:38.643 --> 00:19:41.908
I remember that feeling
from Do Luc.


00:19:41.946 --> 00:19:44.574
You don't forget that.


00:19:48.619 --> 00:19:51.213
- What did you say the next town is?


00:19:51.255 --> 00:19:53.189
Gatlin.


00:19:53.224 --> 00:19:54.953
Does it look big enough
to have a police station?


00:19:54.992 --> 00:19:58.257
No, it's just a dot.


00:19:59.463 --> 00:20:02.057
That little boy was on foot, right?


00:20:02.099 --> 00:20:03.999
Gatlin is the only town for 80 miles.


00:20:04.035 --> 00:20:07.436
- He must have come from there.
- If you say so.


00:20:15.613 --> 00:20:18.047
Why? Why would anybody
wanna do that to a little kid?


00:20:18.082 --> 00:20:20.141
I don't know.


00:20:21.385 --> 00:20:23.819
We might get a better idea


00:20:23.854 --> 00:20:26.584
- if we look inside that.
- Hmm?


00:20:26.624 --> 00:20:28.649
Do you really think so?


00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.594
Probably not.


00:20:31.629 --> 00:20:33.324
It's worth a shot.


00:20:33.364 --> 00:20:35.355
Do you wanna open it?


00:20:38.469 --> 00:20:40.369
Okay.


00:20:45.843 --> 00:20:47.470
Hey...


00:20:49.213 --> 00:20:50.976
thanks.


00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:19.273
Didn't we cross a barn
or something back there?


00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.210
No. It was deserted


00:21:21.245 --> 00:21:24.214
no power feeds
from the road...


00:21:24.248 --> 00:21:25.977
no good.


00:21:26.017 --> 00:21:29.145
- I think you see everything.
- Huh.


00:21:29.186 --> 00:21:32.917
It freaks me out sometimes.
It really does.


00:21:32.957 --> 00:21:35.585
I just feel as if
this is my responsibility, Vicky.


00:21:35.626 --> 00:21:39.323
I hit him, even if he was
bleeding to death when I did.


00:21:39.363 --> 00:21:41.797
- You see, I don't see everything.


00:21:41.832 --> 00:21:45.632
I sure didn't see him.
I took my eyes off the road.


00:21:49.106 --> 00:21:52.234
We haven't seen a car
or a truck in like an hour.


00:21:52.276 --> 00:21:53.538
It's weird.


00:21:53.577 --> 00:21:55.841
Maybe Nebraska's playing
a home game.


00:21:57.214 --> 00:21:59.546
Why don't you tell that
to your American Studies class


00:21:59.583 --> 00:22:01.517
when we get back home?


00:22:01.552 --> 00:22:04.316
"ln Nebraska,
radio hasn't been invented yet."


00:22:04.355 --> 00:22:07.722
- There's nothing at all?
- Zilch.


00:22:07.758 --> 00:22:09.658
The other knot is coming now.


00:22:09.694 --> 00:22:11.685
Atonement!


00:22:11.729 --> 00:22:15.756
Only by the blood
of the lamb are we saved!


00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:18.360
"Atonement" is the word,
brothers and sisters.


00:22:18.402 --> 00:22:20.267
There are some that think...


00:22:20.304 --> 00:22:22.238
No wonder
we're coming in five-by.


00:22:22.273 --> 00:22:24.366
